:"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const [pagination, setPagination] = createTableState({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"function-createtablestate","text":"Function: createTableState()","level":1},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tstate","text":"TState","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"initialvalue","text":"initialValue","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Function: createTableState()\n\n```ts\nfunction createTableState<TState>(initialValue): [() => TState, (updater) => void];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-table/src/createTableState.svelte.ts:18](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/svelte-table/src/createTableState.svelte.ts#L18)\n\nCreates a small Svelte 5 state holder that accepts TanStack Table updaters.\n\nThis is useful when a table state slice should be owned outside the table\nwith `$state`, but still needs to accept both value and functional updater\nforms from `on[State]Change` callbacks.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TState\n\n`TState`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### initialValue\n\n`TState`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[() => `TState`, (`updater`) => `void`\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst [pagination, setPagination] = createTableState({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createTableState\ntitle: createTableState\n---\n\n# Function: createTableState()\n\n```ts\nfunction createTableState<TState>(initialValue): [() => TState, (updater) => void];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-table/src/createTableState.svelte.ts:18](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/svelte-table/src/createTableState.svelte.ts#L18)\n\nCreates a small Svelte 5 state holder that accepts TanStack Table updaters.\n\nThis is useful when a table state slice should be owned outside the table\nwith `$state`, but still needs to accept both value and functional updater\nforms from `on[State]Change` callbacks.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TState\n\n`TState`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### initialValue\n\n`TState`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[() => `TState`, (`updater`) => `void`\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst [pagination, setPagination] = createTableState({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n```\n"}
